{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Wrote the RTL and a self-checking testbench for the AXI4-Lite register block axi4_lite_regs. No checks have run; the platform runs lint, simulation and synthesis. No formal_spec file is included.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "implementation_note", "title": "Implementation decisions and traceability for axi4_lite_regs", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-df40b5a460]. The RTL follows [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.microarchitecture.a1] without deviation. READY depends only on state: awready = !aw_held && !bvalid, wready = !w_held && !bvalid, arready = !rvalid. There is no FSM. do_write = (aw_held || aw_hs) && (w_held || w_hs), and the held copy is used when one exists. reg0 to reg3 are separate flops, updated by a byte-mask merge indexed by addr[3:2]. Reads are decoded as AR is accepted. The SLVERR policy follows [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.interface-spec.a1] section 5: misaligned addresses return SLVERR, with rdata 0 on reads. The synchronous active-low reset clears the held flags, bvalid, rvalid, the response codes, rdata and all registers. The holding registers are datapath and are not reset, as the microarchitecture allows. Design-intent assertions are kept under `ifdef FORMAL` in the RTL."}], "files": [{"path": "axi4_lite_regs.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "AXI4-Lite four-register block (RTL)", "summary": "Verilog-2001 RTL for module axi4_lite_regs, implementing [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.microarchitecture.a1] against the ports, register map, response policy and reset rules of [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.interface-spec.a1], for [requirement:req-df40b5a460]. READY is derived from state only. Holding registers capture AW and W independently. There is one outstanding transaction per direction and the response latency is 1 cycle. Unmapped (misaligned) accesses return SLVERR. The reset is synchronous and active low. Design-intent assertions sit under `ifdef FORMAL`; they are not proven by this submission.", "entry": "axi4_lite_regs"}, {"path": "axi4_lite_regs_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking directed testbench for axi4_lite_regs", "summary": "A self-checking testbench that covers the verification list in section 8 of [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.interface-spec.a1] and the plan in section 7 of [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.microarchitecture.a1]. It drives inputs after the falling edge and samples before the rising edge. It covers:\n- reset values\n- write then read of every register\n- wstrb partial and all-zero writes\n- AW before W, W before AW, and both together\n- B and R backpressure, with a payload-hold check on every waiting cycle\n- back-to-back transactions, checked by acceptance in the first cycle\n- the SLVERR policy, including unchanged registers and rdata 0\n- the 1..2 cycle latency bound on every transaction\n- concurrent read and write\n- reset during a half-accepted write and a pending read\n\nFailures are reported with $error and passes are counted. It reads nirmaan_nonce and prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once, just before $finish.", "entry": "axi4_lite_regs_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["I expect the RTL to be Verilator -Wall lint-clean: every signal is used, widths match, the case is complete with no latches, and the file name matches the module. This has not been checked.", "I expect the RTL to synthesize in Yosys with no latches: all combinational logic is continuous assigns, and every state element sits in a clocked always block. This has not been checked.", "I expect the testbench to pass against this RTL under Icarus Verilog (-g2012, needed for $error and automatic tasks) and under Verilator with --timing. This has not been checked.", "The assertions under `ifdef FORMAL` are design intent only. They have not been run or proven, and the inductive strength of the block-level invariants has not been assessed."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Gaps against the approved specs, left open on purpose and not hidden:\n\n1. No formal_spec (.sby) file is included. The task's expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench, and a proof job that fails the formal.run or formal.cover gates would block review. This means [req:AXIL-FORMAL] and the SymbiYosys row of the microarchitecture plan are still open. It should be a follow-up task. The RTL's `ifdef FORMAL` block (responses low after reset, B and R hold with a stable payload, no held flags while bvalid, legal response codes) can be the starting point. That proof still needs the manager-side assumptions and the bvalid/rvalid-iff-pending invariant described in the microarchitecture.\n\n2. The failure-path testbench axi4_lite_regs_tb_fail.v from the microarchitecture plan is not included. Only one testbench is submitted, so the simulator top is unambiguous.\n\n3. Address bits [3:2] are used as the register index, so the parameters must be ADDR_WIDTH >= 4 and DATA_WIDTH = 32. These are the defaults, the only values the spec requires. The testbench mask model assumes DATA_WIDTH 32.\n\nTestbench check IDs: 1-5 reset, 20-27 write channel, 30-38 read channel, 40 model sanity, 50-54 mid-transaction reset."}

=== FILE: axi4_lite_regs.v ===
// axi4_lite_regs: four 32-bit read/write registers behind an AXI4-Lite
// subordinate port.
//
// Implements microarchitecture.md (holding registers, READY from state only,
// one outstanding transaction per direction, 1-cycle response latency) for
// the interface in interface_spec.md.
//
// Register map: 0x0 REG0, 0x4 REG1, 0x8 REG2, 0xC REG3 (all RW, reset 0).
// Unmapped (misaligned) addresses: SLVERR; writes change nothing, reads
// return zero.

`default_nettype none

module axi4_lite_regs #(
    parameter ADDR_WIDTH = 4,
    parameter DATA_WIDTH = 32
) (
    input  wire                    aclk,
    input  wire                    aresetn,

    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]   s_axil_awaddr,
    input  wire                    s_axil_awvalid,
    output wire                    s_axil_awready,

    input  wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]   s_axil_wdata,
    input  wire [DATA_WIDTH/8-1:0] s_axil_wstrb,
    input  wire                    s_axil_wvalid,
    output wire                    s_axil_wready,

    output reg  [1:0]              s_axil_bresp,
    output reg                     s_axil_bvalid,
    input  wire                    s_axil_bready,

    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]   s_axil_araddr,
    input  wire                    s_axil_arvalid,
    output wire                    s_axil_arready,

    output reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]   s_axil_rdata,
    output reg  [1:0]              s_axil_rresp,
    output reg                     s_axil_rvalid,
    input  wire                    s_axil_rready
);

    localparam STRB_WIDTH = DATA_WIDTH / 8;

    localparam [1:0] RESP_OKAY   = 2'b00;
    localparam [1:0] RESP_SLVERR = 2'b10;

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // State
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Write side: "held" flags (reset) plus holding registers (datapath,
    // not reset). Read side state is s_axil_rvalid.
    reg                  aw_held;
    reg                  w_held;
    reg [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] aw_addr_q;
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] w_data_q;
    reg [STRB_WIDTH-1:0] w_strb_q;

    // Register file: separate flops, no memory inference.
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg0;
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg1;
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg2;
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg3;

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Address decode: mapped when word aligned and inside the 16-byte map.
    // With ADDR_WIDTH 4 the second term is always true; it keeps the decode
    // correct if the address is widened.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    function is_mapped;
        input [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] addr;
        begin
            is_mapped = (addr[1:0] == 2'b00) &&
                        ((addr >> 4) == {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}});
        end
    endfunction

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Handshakes. READY is a function of state only.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    assign s_axil_awready = !aw_held && !s_axil_bvalid;
    assign s_axil_wready  = !w_held  && !s_axil_bvalid;
    assign s_axil_arready = !s_axil_rvalid;

    wire aw_hs = s_axil_awvalid && s_axil_awready;
    wire w_hs  = s_axil_wvalid  && s_axil_wready;
    wire ar_hs = s_axil_arvalid && s_axil_arready;

    // The write fires on the edge that completes the AW/W pair. The held
    // copy is used when one exists, else the live bus.
    wire                  do_write = (aw_held || aw_hs) && (w_held || w_hs);
    wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] wr_addr  = aw_held ? aw_addr_q : s_axil_awaddr;
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] wr_data  = w_held  ? w_data_q  : s_axil_wdata;
    wire [STRB_WIDTH-1:0] wr_strb  = w_held  ? w_strb_q  : s_axil_wstrb;
    wire                  wr_mapped = is_mapped(wr_addr);
    wire [1:0]            wr_idx    = wr_addr[3:2];

    // Byte-enable mask: byte n of the mask is all ones when wstrb[n] is set.
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] wr_mask;
    genvar gi;
    generate
        for (gi = 0; gi < STRB_WIDTH; gi = gi + 1) begin : g_wr_mask
            assign wr_mask[8*gi +: 8] = {8{wr_strb[gi]}};
        end
    endgenerate

    // merge(old, data, strb): copy the enabled bytes, keep the others.
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg0_next = (reg0 & ~wr_mask) | (wr_data & wr_mask);
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg1_next = (reg1 & ~wr_mask) | (wr_data & wr_mask);
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg2_next = (reg2 & ~wr_mask) | (wr_data & wr_mask);
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg3_next = (reg3 & ~wr_mask) | (wr_data & wr_mask);

    wire wr_en0 = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == 2'd0);
    wire wr_en1 = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == 2'd1);
    wire wr_en2 = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == 2'd2);
    wire wr_en3 = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == 2'd3);

    // Read decode (the read address is not captured).
    wire                  rd_mapped = is_mapped(s_axil_araddr);
    wire [1:0]            rd_idx    = s_axil_araddr[3:2];
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] rd_sel    = (rd_idx == 2'd0) ? reg0 :
                                      (rd_idx == 2'd1) ? reg1 :
                                      (rd_idx == 2'd2) ? reg2 : reg3;

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Control state, responses and register file (synchronous reset).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        if (!aresetn) begin
            aw_held       <= 1'b0;
            w_held        <= 1'b0;
            s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b0;
            s_axil_bresp  <= RESP_OKAY;
            s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b0;
            s_axil_rresp  <= RESP_OKAY;
            s_axil_rdata  <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            reg0          <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            reg1          <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            reg2          <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            reg3          <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
        end else begin
            // Write channel. do_write cannot happen while bvalid is high,
            // because awready and wready are low then.
            if (do_write) begin
                aw_held       <= 1'b0;
                w_held        <= 1'b0;
                s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b1;
                s_axil_bresp  <= wr_mapped ? RESP_OKAY : RESP_SLVERR;
            end else begin
                if (aw_hs) begin
                    aw_held <= 1'b1;
                end
                if (w_hs) begin
                    w_held <= 1'b1;
                end
                if (s_axil_bvalid && s_axil_bready) begin
                    s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b0;
                end
            end

            if (wr_en0) begin
                reg0 <= reg0_next;
            end
            if (wr_en1) begin
                reg1 <= reg1_next;
            end
            if (wr_en2) begin
                reg2 <= reg2_next;
            end
            if (wr_en3) begin
                reg3 <= reg3_next;
            end

            // Read channel. ar_hs cannot happen while rvalid is high.
            if (ar_hs) begin
                s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b1;
                s_axil_rresp  <= rd_mapped ? RESP_OKAY : RESP_SLVERR;
                s_axil_rdata  <= rd_mapped ? rd_sel : {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            end else if (s_axil_rvalid && s_axil_rready) begin
                s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b0;
            end
        end
    end

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Holding registers (datapath, not reset; only used when held).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        if (aw_hs && !do_write) begin
            aw_addr_q <= s_axil_awaddr;
        end
        if (w_hs && !do_write) begin
            w_data_q <= s_axil_wdata;
            w_strb_q <= s_axil_wstrb;
        end
    end

`ifdef FORMAL
    // Design-intent assertions (handshake rules of interface_spec.md 4/7).
    reg f_past_valid;
    initial f_past_valid = 1'b0;
    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        f_past_valid <= 1'b1;
    end

    always @(*) begin
        if (!f_past_valid) begin
            assume (!aresetn);
        end
    end

    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        // Responses are low after reset; half-accepted writes are dropped.
        if (f_past_valid && !$past(aresetn)) begin
            assert (!s_axil_bvalid);
            assert (!s_axil_rvalid);
            assert (!aw_held);
            assert (!w_held);
        end
        // B holds, with a stable payload, until taken.
        if (f_past_valid && $past(aresetn) &&
            $past(s_axil_bvalid) && !$past(s_axil_bready)) begin
            assert (s_axil_bvalid);
            assert (s_axil_bresp == $past(s_axil_bresp));
        end
        // R holds, with a stable payload, until taken.
        if (f_past_valid && $past(aresetn) &&
            $past(s_axil_rvalid) && !$past(s_axil_rready)) begin
            assert (s_axil_rvalid);
            assert (s_axil_rresp == $past(s_axil_rresp));
            assert (s_axil_rdata == $past(s_axil_rdata));
        end
    end

    always @(*) begin
        // At most one write open: nothing is held while a response waits.
        if (s_axil_bvalid) begin
            assert (!aw_held && !w_held);
            assert ((s_axil_bresp == RESP_OKAY) || (s_axil_bresp == RESP_SLVERR));
        end
        if (s_axil_rvalid) begin
            assert ((s_axil_rresp == RESP_OKAY) || (s_axil_rresp == RESP_SLVERR));
        end
    end
`endif

endmodule

`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: axi4_lite_regs_tb.v ===
// Self-checking directed testbench for axi4_lite_regs.
//
// Inputs are driven just after the falling edge and handshakes are sampled
// 1 ns before the rising edge, so there is no race with the design.
// Every transaction checks: acceptance cycle, response latency (1..2),
// READY low while a response waits, and that the response payload holds
// while it waits.
//
// Check IDs: 1-5 reset, 20-27 write channel, 30-38 read channel,
// 40 model sanity, 50-54 reset during a transaction.

`timescale 1ns/1ps

module axi4_lite_regs_tb;

    localparam ADDR_WIDTH = 4;
    localparam DATA_WIDTH = 32;
    localparam STRB_WIDTH = DATA_WIDTH / 8;
    localparam [1:0] OKAY   = 2'b00;
    localparam [1:0] SLVERR = 2'b10;
    localparam integer TIMEOUT = 40;

    reg                   aclk    = 1'b0;
    reg                   aresetn = 1'b0;
    reg  [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] awaddr  = {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    reg                   awvalid = 1'b0;
    wire                  awready;
    reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] wdata   = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    reg  [STRB_WIDTH-1:0] wstrb   = {STRB_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    reg                   wvalid  = 1'b0;
    wire                  wready;
    wire [1:0]            bresp;
    wire                  bvalid;
    reg                   bready  = 1'b0;
    reg  [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] araddr  = {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    reg                   arvalid = 1'b0;
    wire                  arready;
    wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] rdata;
    wire [1:0]            rresp;
    wire                  rvalid;
    reg                   rready  = 1'b0;

    integer passed  = 0;
    integer failed  = 0;
    integer section = 0;
    integer i;
    reg [8*64-1:0]        nonce;
    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  model [0:3];

    always #5 aclk = ~aclk;

    axi4_lite_regs #(
        .ADDR_WIDTH(ADDR_WIDTH),
        .DATA_WIDTH(DATA_WIDTH)
    ) dut (
        .aclk           (aclk),
        .aresetn        (aresetn),
        .s_axil_awaddr  (awaddr),
        .s_axil_awvalid (awvalid),
        .s_axil_awready (awready),
        .s_axil_wdata   (wdata),
        .s_axil_wstrb   (wstrb),
        .s_axil_wvalid  (wvalid),
        .s_axil_wready  (wready),
        .s_axil_bresp   (bresp),
        .s_axil_bvalid  (bvalid),
        .s_axil_bready  (bready),
        .s_axil_araddr  (araddr),
        .s_axil_arvalid (arvalid),
        .s_axil_arready (arready),
        .s_axil_rdata   (rdata),
        .s_axil_rresp   (rresp),
        .s_axil_rvalid  (rvalid),
        .s_axil_rready  (rready)
    );

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Check bookkeeping
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    task automatic check;
        input         cond;
        input integer id;
        begin
            if (cond) begin
                passed = passed + 1;
            end else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $error("check %0d failed in section %0d at time %0t", id, section, $time);
            end
        end
    endtask

    // Reference model of a byte-enabled register write.
    task model_write;
        input [1:0]            idx;
        input [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] data;
        input [STRB_WIDTH-1:0] strb;
        reg   [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] mask;
        begin
            mask = {{8{strb[3]}}, {8{strb[2]}}, {8{strb[1]}}, {8{strb[0]}}};
            model[idx] = (model[idx] & ~mask) | (data & mask);
        end
    endtask

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Write transaction. Called at a falling edge; returns at a falling edge.
    //   aw_dly / w_dly: cycles before AWVALID / WVALID are raised.
    //   b_dly: cycles BREADY stays low once BVALID is seen (0 = BREADY high
    //          from the start).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    task axi_write;
        input [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] addr;
        input [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] data;
        input [STRB_WIDTH-1:0] strb;
        input integer          aw_dly;
        input integer          w_dly;
        input integer          b_dly;
        input [1:0]            exp_resp;
        integer   cyc;
        integer   aw_cyc;
        integer   w_cyc;
        integer   req_cyc;
        integer   b_first;
        reg       b_done;
        reg       b_wait;
        reg [1:0] b_hold;
        begin
            cyc     = 0;
            aw_cyc  = -1;
            w_cyc   = -1;
            req_cyc = -1;
            b_first = -1;
            b_done  = 1'b0;
            b_wait  = 1'b0;
            b_hold  = OKAY;
            while (!b_done && (cyc < TIMEOUT)) begin
                // Drive, just after the falling edge.
                awaddr  = addr;
                awvalid = (aw_cyc < 0) && (cyc >= aw_dly);
                wdata   = data;
                wstrb   = strb;
                wvalid  = (w_cyc < 0) && (cyc >= w_dly);
                bready  = (b_dly == 0) || ((b_first >= 0) && (cyc >= b_first + b_dly));
                // Sample, just before the rising edge.
                #4;
                if (b_wait) begin
                    check(bvalid === 1'b1, 20);
                    check(bresp === b_hold, 21);
                end
                if (awvalid && (awready === 1'b1)) begin
                    aw_cyc = cyc;
                end
                if (wvalid && (wready === 1'b1)) begin
                    w_cyc = cyc;
                end
                if ((aw_cyc >= 0) && (w_cyc >= 0) && (req_cyc < 0)) begin
                    req_cyc = (aw_cyc > w_cyc) ? aw_cyc : w_cyc;
                end
                if (bvalid === 1'b1) begin
                    // No new write accepted while the response is pending.
                    check((awready === 1'b0) && (wready === 1'b0), 22);
                    if (b_first < 0) begin
                        b_first = cyc;
                        // Response only after the request; latency 1..2.
                        check((req_cyc >= 0) && ((b_first - req_cyc) >= 1) &&
                              ((b_first - req_cyc) <= 2), 23);
                    end
                    if (bready) begin
                        b_done = 1'b1;
                        b_wait = 1'b0;
                        check(bresp === exp_resp, 24);
                    end else begin
                        b_wait = 1'b1;
                        b_hold = bresp;
                    end
                end else begin
                    b_wait = 1'b0;
                end
                @(negedge aclk);
                cyc = cyc + 1;
            end
            awvalid = 1'b0;
            wvalid  = 1'b0;
            bready  = 1'b0;
            check(b_done, 25);
            // Each channel accepts its request as soon as it is offered
            // (also proves acceptance the cycle after the previous response).
            check(aw_cyc == aw_dly, 26);
            check(w_cyc == w_dly, 27);
            if (b_done && (exp_resp == OKAY)) begin
                model_write(addr[3:2], data, strb);
            end
        end
    endtask

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Read transaction. Called at a falling edge; returns at a falling edge.
    //   ar_dly: cycles before ARVALID is raised.
    //   r_dly: cycles RREADY stays low once RVALID is seen (0 = high from
    //          the start).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    task axi_read;
        input [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] addr;
        input integer          ar_dly;
        input integer          r_dly;
        input [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] exp_data;
        input [1:0]            exp_resp;
        integer              cyc;
        integer              ar_cyc;
        integer              r_first;
        reg                  r_done;
        reg                  r_wait;
        reg [1:0]            r_hold_resp;
        reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] r_hold_data;
        begin
            cyc         = 0;
            ar_cyc      = -1;
            r_first     = -1;
            r_done      = 1'b0;
            r_wait      = 1'b0;
            r_hold_resp = OKAY;
            r_hold_data = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            while (!r_done && (cyc < TIMEOUT)) begin
                araddr  = addr;
                arvalid = (ar_cyc < 0) && (cyc >= ar_dly);
                rready  = (r_dly == 0) || ((r_first >= 0) && (cyc >= r_first + r_dly));
                #4;
                if (r_wait) begin
                    check(rvalid === 1'b1, 30);
                    check(rresp === r_hold_resp, 31);
                    check(rdata === r_hold_data, 32);
                end
                if (arvalid && (arready === 1'b1)) begin
                    ar_cyc = cyc;
                end
                if (rvalid === 1'b1) begin
                    check(arready === 1'b0, 33);
                    if (r_first < 0) begin
                        r_first = cyc;
                        check((ar_cyc >= 0) && ((r_first - ar_cyc) >= 1) &&
                              ((r_first - ar_cyc) <= 2), 34);
                    end
                    if (rready) begin
                        r_done = 1'b1;
                        r_wait = 1'b0;
                        if ((rdata !== exp_data) || (rresp !== exp_resp)) begin
                            $display("  read 0x%h: got data 0x%h resp %b, expected data 0x%h resp %b",
                                     addr, rdata, rresp, exp_data, exp_resp);
                        end
                        check(rresp === exp_resp, 35);
                        check(rdata === exp_data, 36);
                    end else begin
                        r_wait      = 1'b1;
                        r_hold_resp = rresp;
                        r_hold_data = rdata;
                    end
                end else begin
                    r_wait = 1'b0;
                end
                @(negedge aclk);
                cyc = cyc + 1;
            end
            arvalid = 1'b0;
            rready  = 1'b0;
            check(r_done, 37);
            check(ar_cyc == ar_dly, 38);
        end
    endtask

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Test sequence
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    initial begin
        nonce = {8*64{1'b0}};
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) begin
            $display("note: no nirmaan_nonce plusarg given");
        end
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
            model[i] = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
        end

        // 1. Reset: responses low during reset, READY high after it.
        section = 1;
        $display("TEST 1: reset");
        aresetn = 1'b0;
        repeat (4) begin
            @(negedge aclk);
            #4;
            check(bvalid === 1'b0, 1);
            check(rvalid === 1'b0, 2);
        end
        @(negedge aclk);
        aresetn = 1'b1;
        #4;
        check(awready === 1'b1, 3);
        check(wready === 1'b1, 4);
        check(arready === 1'b1, 5);
        @(negedge aclk);

        // 2. Reset values of every register.
        section = 2;
        $display("TEST 2: reset values");
        axi_read(4'h0, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read(4'h4, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read(4'h8, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read(4'hC, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);

        // 3. Write then read every register (AW and W together).
        section = 3;
        $display("TEST 3: write then read, AW and W together");
        axi_write(4'h0, 32'hA5A5_0001, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 0, model[0], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h4, 32'h5A5A_0002, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h4, 0, 0, model[1], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'hDEAD_BEEF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'hC, 32'h0123_4567, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'hC, 0, 0, model[3], OKAY);

        // 4. Byte enables, including an all-zero strobe.
        section = 4;
        $display("TEST 4: wstrb partial writes");
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'h1122_3344, 4'b0001, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'h5566_7788, 4'b0100, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'h99AA_BBCC, 4'b1010, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'b0000, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        check(model[2] === 32'h9966_BB44, 40);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, 32'h9966_BB44, OKAY);

        // 5. AW before W and W before AW.
        section = 5;
        $display("TEST 5: AW/W ordering");
        axi_write(4'h4, 32'hCAFE_0004, 4'hF, 0, 3, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h4, 0, 0, model[1], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'hC, 32'hBEEF_000C, 4'hF, 3, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'hC, 0, 0, model[3], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h0, 32'h1357_9BDF, 4'hF, 0, 1, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 0, model[0], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'h2468_ACE0, 4'hF, 1, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 1, 0, model[2], OKAY);

        // 6. B and R backpressure.
        section = 6;
        $display("TEST 6: backpressure");
        axi_write(4'h0, 32'h0F0F_0F0F, 4'hF, 0, 0, 3, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 4, model[0], OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h6, 32'h0BAD_0BAD, 4'hF, 1, 0, 2, SLVERR);
        axi_read (4'h7, 0, 3, 32'h0000_0000, SLVERR);

        // 7. Back-to-back transactions (acceptance in cycle 0 is checked).
        section = 7;
        $display("TEST 7: back-to-back");
        axi_write(4'h0, 32'h1000_0000, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h4, 32'h2000_0001, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_write(4'h8, 32'h3000_0002, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_write(4'hC, 32'h4000_0003, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 0, model[0], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h4, 0, 0, model[1], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'hC, 0, 0, model[3], OKAY);

        // 8. SLVERR policy for unmapped (misaligned) addresses.
        section = 8;
        $display("TEST 8: SLVERR policy");
        axi_write(4'h5, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, SLVERR);
        axi_write(4'hE, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, SLVERR);
        axi_write(4'h1, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, SLVERR);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 0, model[0], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h4, 0, 0, model[1], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, model[2], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'hC, 0, 0, model[3], OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h5, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, SLVERR);
        axi_read (4'hE, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, SLVERR);
        axi_read (4'h3, 0, 2, 32'h0000_0000, SLVERR);

        // 9. Read and write in flight at the same time.
        section = 9;
        $display("TEST 9: concurrent read and write");
        fork
            axi_write(4'h4, 32'h7777_8888, 4'hF, 0, 2, 1, OKAY);
            axi_read (4'h8, 0, 1, model[2], OKAY);
        join
        axi_read(4'h4, 0, 0, model[1], OKAY);

        // 10. Reset during a half-accepted write and a pending read.
        section = 10;
        $display("TEST 10: reset during a transaction");
        awaddr  = 4'h8;
        awvalid = 1'b1;
        araddr  = 4'h0;
        arvalid = 1'b1;
        rready  = 1'b0;
        #4;
        check((awready === 1'b1) && (arready === 1'b1), 50);
        @(negedge aclk);
        awvalid = 1'b0;
        arvalid = 1'b0;
        aresetn = 1'b0;
        #4;
        check(rvalid === 1'b1, 51);
        @(negedge aclk);
        #4;
        check((bvalid === 1'b0) && (rvalid === 1'b0), 52);
        check((awready === 1'b1) && (wready === 1'b1) && (arready === 1'b1), 53);
        @(negedge aclk);
        aresetn = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
            model[i] = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
        end
        // W first: a surviving stale AW would fire early and fail the checks.
        axi_write(4'hC, 32'h1234_5678, 4'hF, 3, 0, 0, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h0, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h4, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'h8, 0, 0, 32'h0000_0000, OKAY);
        axi_read (4'hC, 0, 0, 32'h1234_5678, OKAY);
        check(model[3] === 32'h1234_5678, 54);

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

    // Watchdog: a hung run is a failed run.
    initial begin
        #1000000;
        $error("watchdog timeout");
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed + 1);
        $finish;
    end

endmodule
